  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The review notes that the actual city-wide contribution and spatial distribution of balcony gardens remain unmeasured because existing literature rarely treats them as formal urban green spaces.",
      "what": "A scoping review of 160 studies synthesizes current knowledge on the contributions of resident-led balcony gardens to urban environments. The analysis reveals that these micro-spaces improve physical and mental health, foster social interaction, mitigate heat, enhance air quality, and support urban biodiversity.",
      "why": "It establishes balcony gardens as a distinct category of decentralized, resident-led green infrastructure, shifting the focus from large public parks to the unmapped ecological and social contributions of private micro-spaces in dense cities."
    }
